cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this proof of concept, please cite it as below, and cite the original paper it replicates."
title: "Channel Decomposition of Political Ads: a proof of concept"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rej
    given-names: Aleksander
    affiliation: "University of Warsaw"
date-released: 2026-09-25
version: "2"
license: MIT
url: "https://arejgh.github.io/channel-decomposition-poc/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ARejGH/channel-decomposition-poc"
abstract: >-
  Independent student proof of concept: a mini-replication of selected measurement steps of
  Ciccarone (2026) on 22 political ads, extended with an omni embedder and an exact three-player
  Shapley decomposition of image, prosody and text channels. Built with an agentic AI workflow in
  zen-system, the author's agent harness (models used in the replication: Claude Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra);
  not peer-reviewed; not affiliated with or endorsed by the original author.
keywords:
  - political advertising
  - multimodal embeddings
  - replication
  - agentic AI
references:
